@flexiarg buffer-cleaner/observe-categories
@title Observe Categories
@keywords observe, channel, category, decisiveness
@audience adapter, G computation
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade technique
@provenance v3 diagram chip 1 (cascade-policy-example.html); category set = futon-buffer-cleaner.el candidate-kind predicates (:130-179). Node semantics: read the real buffer state and tag each buffer with its observation channel.
@class process
@domain process
@status adapter node, 2026-09-15; params in nodes/observe-categories.params.edn

! conclusion:
  Each buffer arrives tagged with its category (the cleaner's own
  predicates) and the channel's decisiveness class; nothing is killed
  or judged here.

  + THEN: emit {:name :kind :file :modified :process-gone
    :visible :display-age-seconds} per buffer, read-only.

  + BECAUSE: the observation model's per-channel honesty begins here —
    a decisive channel must be declared decisive at observation, not
    discounted later in the score.
